                           ffsim/gpu/make_train_gpu.py (32 patches for CUDA/CPU
                           and a virtual charged clock; see
                           ffsim/gpu/PATCH_NOTES.md)

Changes made in the two recipes, relative to the organiser baseline:
architecture (depth/width, grouped-query attention with one KV head, value
embeddings, LeakyReLU^2 MLP, attention-source reuse, key offset, multi-token
prediction), optimizer and schedule (Muon/AdamW scaling, fused Newton-Schulz,
ZeRO sharding, batch warm-up, charged-clock cooldown, EMA blend and prewarm),
data sampling (row pool) and many throughput changes. Each file's header
docstring states that it is derived from the organiser baseline. The recipe files
are byte-identical to the files we uploaded to the challenge (sha256 in
recipes/README.md), so no further notice was inserted into them.

The organiser's prepare.py, README, tokenizer and data are not redistributed.

